From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:51:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Log every strategy decision (BUY/SELL/HOLD), not just trades

Zero visibility into whether the once-daily decision window was
actually firing at all - the only way to tell 'decided HOLD for every
symbol' apart from 'the decision logic never ran' was to look for
resulting trades, and both cases look identical from the outside (no
trades either way). Reported today: 3 days with no trades and no way
to confirm whether that's genuinely no signals firing (statistically
plausible - ~18-20% chance of a random 3-day zero-trade stretch given
expected trade frequency) or the decision window silently not running.

Added an INFO log line for every decision (not just BUY/SELL) showing
the symbol, signal, price, holding, and date. Going forward, checking
logs around the 15:20-15:30 IST decision window will show either a
full set of HOLD decisions (confirming the logic ran, just no signals
triggered - expected/fine) or nothing at all (confirming an actual
bug worth investigating), instead of both cases looking identical.
---
 app/bot_runner.py | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/bot_runner.py b/app/bot_runner.py
index 8200985..b5822d5 100644
--- a/app/bot_runner.py
+++ b/app/bot_runner.py
@@ -286,6 +286,10 @@ class BotRunner:
                     signal = self.strategies[symbol].decide(price, holding)
                     self.last_signal[symbol] = signal
                     self.last_decision_date[symbol] = today_str
+                    logger.info(
+                        f"Decision for {symbol} (user_id={self.user_id}): {signal} "
+                        f"(price={price}, holding={holding}, date={today_str})"
+                    )
                     if signal == "BUY":
                         # Size like engine.py does: capital_pct_per_trade of
                         # current cash, not a fixed share count. This is the
